-- S23 Maharashtra prose — pali-raigad (Ballaleshwar)
-- Verdict matrix: 6 go / 3 skip / 3 wait
-- Anchors: 1810 Nana Phadnis stone reconstruction; only named-deity Ashtavinayak (Ballal the devotee);
--          Konkan/Raigad 3500-4000mm monsoon; Khopoli-Pali 30km via Mumbai-Pune Expressway;
--          Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12 + Anant Chaturdashi Sep 22; Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4 2026;
--          two main idols (east + north facing); 8th + final temple in Ashtavinayak yatra protocol.

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('pali-raigad', 1, 'go', 4, 'Pali sits on the Konkan side of the Ashtavinayak circuit, 110km from Pune via the Mumbai-Pune Expressway and Khopoli exit. January delivers the cleanest window on the Konkan plateau — 18-28C, low humidity by Raigad standards, and the post-Margashirsha pilgrim crush has thinned. Ballaleshwar, the only Ashtavinayak whose deity carries a personal name (Ballal, the boy devotee), sits in its 1810 Nana Phadnis stone reconstruction with two principal idols: one east-facing in the inner sanctum, one north-facing in the outer hall. Morning aarti runs 5:00am-5:30am; pradakshina pavements are cool until 11am. Weekend MTDC and MSRTC yatra buses from Pune-Swargate use January as their soft-launch month before the Magh peak — book seats two weeks ahead, lodging two days.', 'Mild Konkan winter, low humidity, and post-festival temple calm make January the most workable single-temple day-trip month before the Magh Ganesh Jayanti wave arrives in early February.', NULL),
('pali-raigad', 2, 'go', 5, 'February is Pali''s strongest single month after September. Maghi Ganesh Jayanti falls Wed Feb 4 2026 (Magh Shukla Chaturthi) — the secondary all-India Ganesh anniversary, and every Ashtavinayak runs a 3-day mahotsav around it with palki processions, abhishek at 4am, and dindi groups walking in from Khopoli station. Weather holds steady at 18-30C with the Konkan haze still soft. The temple''s two-idol arrangement is fully open for darshan on Feb 4; sone-paan offerings cost ₹251 at the trust counter. The traffic spike runs Feb 2-6; outside that window the temple is quiet enough to read the 1810 Phadnis inscription panels carefully. Pune-Pali day-tripping needs an early 5am start to clear Khopoli ghat traffic.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4 2026 lights up the temple''s secondary mahotsav with palki, dawn abhishek, and full dindi presence; weather still holds Konkan-mild before March humidity creeps in.', NULL),
('pali-raigad', 3, 'go', 4, 'March is the last clean month on the Konkan before pre-monsoon humidity loads in. Daytime climbs 30-34C but mornings stay 20-22C through to mid-month. The temple campus is quiet — no major Ganesh anchor in March on the Marathi calendar — and Pali''s 1810 stonework photographs at its sharpest in the dry, low-haze light. Gudi Padwa falls Mar 19 2026; the Marathi New Year pulls weekend regional traffic into all Ashtavinayak temples for first-darshan rituals between Mar 18-22, but Pali''s Raigad-side location keeps numbers below the Pune-cluster temples. Outside the Gudi Padwa window, this is the best month for solo or small-group yatra without festival-day waits. The Kuthar-Ghatte rivers are dry, so Pali''s landscape feel is austere — basalt outcrops, dry deciduous, no green.', 'Last pre-humid window for clean Konkan light; Gudi Padwa Mar 19 brings Marathi New Year first-darshan crowds Mar 18-22 but the rest of March stays quiet.', NULL),
('pali-raigad', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April is when the Konkan air sets against you. Pali sits in the Raigad belt where coastal humidity meets inland heat — daytime 32-36C with 70-80% humidity makes the pavement pradakshina genuinely oppressive by 10am. Mornings 5-8am still work if you commit to a 4am Pune start. The temple stays open and crowds are at their annual low between festivals, so darshan is fast, but most pilgrims push the yatra into early May before Akshaya Tritiya or wait until September. Hotels in Khopoli and Pali drop weekend rates 30-40%. If you''re doing only Pali (not a multi-temple loop), April mornings are passable; if you''re attempting the full 8-temple yatra with Pali on day 2-3, the cumulative heat fatigue makes it punishing.', 'Mornings 5-8am remain workable and accommodation is at annual lows — for a single-temple Pali day-trip from Pune or Mumbai this is still doable with discipline.', 'Daytime 32-36C combined with 70-80% Konkan humidity makes any after-9am pradakshina or open-courtyard waiting genuinely difficult; full 8-temple yatra accumulates dangerous heat fatigue across day 2.'),
('pali-raigad', 5, 'skip', 2, 'May is the unwise month for Pali. Konkan humidity peaks at 80-85% with daytime 34-38C, and Pali''s temple campus has limited shaded covered space — the prakaram is open-sky. Pavements stay too hot for barefoot pradakshina from 9:30am until 5pm. The temple stays operational and Raigad-side homestays are at deep-discount rates, but heat-stroke risk during multi-hour darshan queues is real. Akshaya Tritiya falls May 1 2026 — a small Marathi anchor that lifts numbers briefly. Mumbai and Pune-side pilgrims time their Ashtavinayak yatra to avoid the entire month; September-November and February are when serious bookings clear. The pre-monsoon Konkan haze also kills photography. Wait for the post-Anant-Chaturdashi October window.', NULL, 'Konkan humidity 80-85% plus 34-38C peak heat makes Pali''s open-courtyard prakaram and barefoot pradakshina genuinely hazardous between 9:30am and 5pm; queue waits in the open accelerate heat stress.'),
('pali-raigad', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks the Konkan southwest monsoon onset over Raigad. The first 7-10 days of June are usually false-start showers driven by the Arabian Sea pre-monsoon convection; by Jun 10-15 the southwest front consolidates and Raigad enters its full 3500-4000mm seasonal wet phase. The Mumbai-Pune Expressway stays open year-round but the Khopoli-Pali state-highway ghat sections see seasonal waterfalls, intermittent mudslides, and 30-60 minute closures during heavy spells. The Ballaleshwar temple stays open all monsoon — darshan never closes — but the broader yatra logistics get punishing. Konkan ferry routes from the Mumbai-side (Mandwa-Alibaug) start curtailing by month-end, which affects multi-stop pilgrims combining Pali with coastal stops at Diveagar or Murud. Early June (Jun 1-10) remains a usable window if showers stay light; the second half flips reliably to monsoon proper.', 'Early June (1-10) can still work if monsoon arrival is late; the landscape begins to green and crowds drop sharply, useful for a single-temple Pali day-trip.', 'After Jun 15 the southwest monsoon consolidates over Raigad with 3500-4000mm seasonal totals; Khopoli ghat closures and ferry curtailment make any multi-stop Ashtavinayak yatra logistics unreliable.'),
('pali-raigad', 7, 'skip', 2, 'July is the deepest monsoon month on the central Konkan and Raigad. Rainfall averages 1000-1200mm for the month alone at Pali — among the heaviest single-month totals anywhere on the Konkan stretch. Khopoli ghat routes flood routinely during the heaviest spells, the Mumbai-Pune Expressway sees fog and aquaplaning warnings on the Khandala-Lonavala descent, and the Pali state highway sees genuine 1-3 day closures when river crossings overtop. Konkan ferry routes from the Mumbai-side are off entirely through July. The Ballaleshwar temple stays open but darshan numbers fall to monthly lows; the local Ashadi-Ekadashi pilgrim flow (Jul 4 2026, Pandharpur Wari) draws Maharashtrian devotees south toward Pandharpur, not toward Ashtavinayak. For Pali specifically, the access risk outweighs any green-landscape photographic upside. Wait for September peak or push to October clarity.', NULL, 'July 1000-1200mm rainfall on Raigad triggers regular ghat closures, expressway aquaplaning, and 1-3 day local highway shutdowns; the temple stays open but reaching it reliably is the problem.'),
('pali-raigad', 8, 'skip', 2, 'August continues the heavy southwest monsoon over Raigad. Rainfall holds at 800-1000mm for the month — still among the highest single-month totals on the central Konkan. Sankashti Chaturthi falls Tue Aug 4 2026 (Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday-aligned auspicious fast day) and brings a small dedicated pilgrim flow despite weather, with palki ceremonies at dawn and full abhishek through the day. Beyond Aug 4 the month is quiet. The same Raigad access problems persist throughout August: Konkan ferry routes still off, intermittent ghat closures on the Khopoli-Pali state highway, and an unreliable last-mile drive from either Khopoli or Mumbai sides. Hardcore Ashtavinayak devotees do undertake the yatra in monsoon as a tapas (austerity) commitment — Pali''s 1810 Phadnis stonework against the green Raigad hills looks remarkable when wet — but for general visitors the logistics are forbidding. Wait for September''s festival peak or October''s post-monsoon calm.', NULL, 'August continues 800-1000mm Raigad rainfall with ghat closures and ferry routes still off; only the Aug 4 Angarki Chaturthi pulls dedicated pilgrims who accept the weather as part of the vow.'),
('pali-raigad', 9, 'go', 5, 'September is Pali''s absolute peak. Ganesh Chaturthi falls Sat Sep 12 2026 (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi), opening the 10-day Ganeshotsav that closes Anant Chaturdashi Tue Sep 22. Ashtavinayak yatra packages run continuously — MTDC, MSRTC, and 30+ private operators flood the circuit with 2-night/3-day buses (₹3500-8000 per pilgrim). Pali sees its highest annual footfall: 30,000-50,000 visitors on the Sep 12 chaturthi day alone, palki processions from neighbouring villages, 18-hour darshan, and continuous abhishek. The Konkan monsoon is in tail phase — Sep 1-15 still wet, Sep 16-30 drying — but Raigad green-up is at peak, basalt hills washed, paddy paddyfields ready for harvest. Book lodging at least 90 days ahead and budget 4-6 hour darshan queues on chaturthi day.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12 to Anant Chaturdashi Sep 22 is the entire reason Ashtavinayak exists in popular pilgrimage memory; Pali sees its annual peak with continuous abhishek, palki, and full yatra-package logistics in motion.', NULL),
('pali-raigad', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is the post-monsoon clarity window every yatra package targets when Sep slots are sold out. The Konkan dries up sharply after Anant Chaturdashi; by Oct 10 the rain stops, Raigad green is at its visual peak, and humidity drops to 60-65% with daytime 28-32C. Temple traffic remains heavy through Oct 15 as overflow from September peak settles, then thins to comfortable. Sharad Purnima falls Oct 25 2026 (Kojagiri) — a Marathi anchor that lifts numbers briefly. The post-monsoon Raigad landscape with paddy harvest, washed basalt, and clear Western Ghats views makes October the best photography month for Pali. Khopoli ghat is fully clear; Konkan ferries restart by Oct 15. This is the ideal compromise month — high spiritual energy residue from September, plus the weather Maghi Feb gives you without the queue intensity.', 'Post-monsoon clarity peaks with washed Raigad basalt, harvest paddy, and 28-32C daytime; temple energy retains Sep festival residue without chaturthi-scale queues — the single best photography and pradakshina month.', NULL),
('pali-raigad', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is Pali''s most comfortable month full stop. Daytime 26-30C, nights 18-22C, near-zero humidity by Konkan standards, and the post-monsoon air is glass-clear. Tulsi Vivah (Nov 1 2026) and Kartik Purnima (Nov 24) anchor the Marathi devotional calendar, both bringing moderate pilgrim flow without the September-scale crush. Pune-side day-trippers fill the temple on weekends; weekday mornings 6-10am are calm enough for prayer, study of the 1810 Phadnis stone inscriptions, and unhurried pradakshina. Yatra-package operators run a secondary high season Nov 15-Dec 15 — book buses 3 weeks ahead. The Konkan green is fading by month-end but the air clarity makes the basalt hills around Pali photograph cleanly. This is the locals-recommend month over Sep for non-festival pilgrims.', 'Clearest air, lowest humidity, and 26-30C daytime make November the locals-recommended Ashtavinayak month for pilgrims who want the spiritual depth without the September crowd intensity.', NULL),
('pali-raigad', 12, 'go', 4, 'December stays mild on the Konkan — 24-30C daytime, 16-20C nights — but is when Pune-Mumbai escape tourism peaks. Yatra package buses run Dec 20-Jan 5 at near-September density as families fold Ashtavinayak into year-end leave. Margashirsha Purnima (Dec 24 2026) is a minor anchor. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tue Dec 1 — auspicious Tuesday fast day for Ganesh devotees, palki ceremony at dawn. Weather is reliable; temple campus stays in its post-monsoon clean state with no festival decoration distraction. Christmas-New Year window (Dec 25-Jan 2) sees Mumbai weekend day-trippers stretch lunch crowds at the trust prasad-bhandar from noon-3pm. Book lodging 30 days ahead for the Dec 20-Jan 5 stretch; off-peak December mid-week (Dec 5-15) is closer to November-quiet.', 'Mild Konkan winter persists with Angarki Chaturthi Dec 1 plus a secondary yatra package season Dec 20-Jan 5; off-peak mid-December stays close to November-quiet for unhurried darshan.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
  score = EXCLUDED.score,
  prose_lead = EXCLUDED.prose_lead,
